Diagnosis: `ORA-06531: Reference to uninitialized collection` comes from the line `l_batch.EXTEND;`. The variable `l_batch` is a nested table, but it has not been initialized. In PL/SQL, a nested table variable is null until it is given a value with its constructor. Calling `EXTEND` on that null nested table raises `ORA-06531`.

Repair: initialize the nested table before calling `EXTEND`. The selected source has no package context, so I am returning it as a standalone function. This proposal has not been compiled or run.

```plsql
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION first_batch RETURN NUMBER IS
  TYPE batch_t IS TABLE OF NUMBER;
  l_batch batch_t := batch_t();
BEGIN
  l_batch.EXTEND;
  l_batch(1) := 17;
  RETURN l_batch(1);
END first_batch;
```

Changed: added `:= batch_t()` to the declaration of `l_batch`. That creates an empty, non-null nested table, so `l_batch.EXTEND` can then add one element.

